{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire","id":134546,"title":"Demond and Prommy (and Vampire)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-12T16:04:09-07:00","id":134546,"title":"Demond and Prommy (and Vampire)","content":"Hello folks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I want try a little of crossover, and have a couple of question: demon can be binded by blood bond? Are they, vulnerable to Disquiet?<br /> Thanks a lot! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:24:57-07:00","id":134615,"title":"","content":"Yes, and yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:36:19-07:00","id":134623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire?p=134615#post134615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No and yes, rather, unless I'm misremembering any changes from Blood and Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:42:47-07:00","id":134637,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't blood binding work? Works on everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:48:01-07:00","id":134643,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all, i think too for a &quot;yes-yes&quot; : on Requiem, blood bond affect only normal human and vampires, but B&amp;S there are no such limitation.<br /> Well, if the developer dont make counter argumantion...i take this question as solved, thanks a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:58:57-07:00","id":134681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire?p=134637#post134637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't blood binding work? Works on everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood-binding, a.k.a. the Vinculum, specifically only works on things along the mortal-to-vampire spectrum. Blood <i>addiction</i> is the supernatural compulsion that the Vitae brings about that isn't affected by template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T17:05:44-07:00","id":134688,"title":"","content":"By no means a counter-point, but a small word of warning: Disquiet can cause to pretty wonky problems in Crossover groups. Indeed my general experience with Disquiet is that players don't always respond super well to &quot;You must now irrationally dislike that guy&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're running with Demons and Prommies side-by-side you may consider coming up with a reason why Demons aren't affected, at least not as severely, by Disquiet. (Their alien mechanical minds operating differently seems a good one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T17:44:03-07:00","id":134714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire?p=134681#post134681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood-binding, a.k.a. the Vinculum, specifically only works on things along the mortal-to-vampire spectrum. Blood <i>addiction</i> is the supernatural compulsion that the Vitae brings about that isn't affected by template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check the FAQ. Blood Bond does work on other supernaturals now, and it didn't expressly forbid it in the book either.<br /> <br /> It came up during the Werewolf Claws/Shapeshifting threads. But Vinculum does work on major templates now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T01:15:36-07:00","id":135103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire?p=134688#post134688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're running with Demons and Prommies side-by-side you may consider coming up with a reason why Demons aren't affected, at least not as severely, by Disquiet. (Their alien mechanical minds operating differently seems a good one).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, the demon and promethean are npc, it was for a main &quot;plot&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T11:35:51-07:00","id":135576,"title":"","content":"I think one of the best simple answers for this is listed under the stereotype quip for Integrator Demons: &quot;Prometheans: I studied under one for almost two weeks before I killed it. I still don\u2019t know why. I learned many useful things, though.&quot; &lt;-- Indicative of Disquiet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T12:54:04-07:00","id":135673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>64bitjedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire?p=135576#post135576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Integrator Demons: &quot;Prometheans: I studied under one for almost two weeks before I killed it. I still don\u2019t know why. I learned many useful things, though.&quot; &lt;-- Indicative of Disquiet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:11:54-07:00","id":135808,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/134546-demond-and-prommy-and-vampire?p=134688#post134688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By no means a counter-point, but a small word of warning: Disquiet can cause to pretty wonky problems in Crossover groups. Indeed my general experience with Disquiet is that players don't always respond super well to &quot;You must now irrationally dislike that guy&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you're running with Demons and Prommies side-by-side you may consider coming up with a reason why Demons aren't affected, at least not as severely, by Disquiet. (Their alien mechanical minds operating differently seems a good one).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yes. But you don't have to say &quot;You must now irrationally dislike that guy&quot;. I am a part of a crossover game where I play a Prommy and the other group members are two Immortals and an Awakened Mage. I am basically an Unfleshed/Nuclear thingie, and my Disquiet manifests as a mix between a very queer, uncanny feeling that something isn't right. That my Promethean isn't being genuine (Like the uncanny valley feeling you get from a near life-like robot) and at later stages, a sense of dread that this <i>person-thing </i>has to be killed, before he kills you. I roleplay the early stages, with roleplay that seems <i>sorta</i> bad, where it seems almost artificial and false. The later stages, I handle via narrative quips here and there. For eksample, they started having dreams, wherein the Mages magic was null against the Promethean, as it brutalised the Mage and burned him in atomic fire. The Immortal couldn't be killed, so she had a dream wherein the machine-man raped her repeadedly and broke every bone in her body over the course of many hours. These dreams were followed up by a scene in which my Promethean lifted a small tank in front of the mage, making him realise that the Promethean was very capable of the things he had seen in his dream, and a scene wherein we had to change cloths and my Promethean stared for an awkwardly long time at the Immortals naked body, making her think that perhaps that dream had a hint of aweful prophecy in it.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Disquiet in crossovers are a tough nut to really crack effectively, and its a hard balancing act between giving it enough narrative focus to make it cool for the Promethean, and sufficiently little so as to not detract from the plot of your chronicle. I can entirely understand if you choose to curb it in your game.<br /> Although i will say, that if you do choose to let Demons be affected by it, it will most likely make your Prometheans experience much more enjoyable. One of the things i truely enjoy about my aformentioned Prommy, is how an unnatural aversion like Disquiet can conflict with the wishes for companionship of a genuinely good and kind individual. That is of course assuming that your Promethean player is up for the challenge of roleplaying it, effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T16:33:02-07:00","id":135871,"title":"","content":"That is the preferred way to handle it, yes. Provide a reason for hate and let the players make the decisions. (By the book it's a compulsion, and by the end they'll have no say.)<br /> <br /> Even so, different strokes for different folks. Not everyone is going to want a scenario in which one of the players will invariably be assaulted by the others. This is one of those &quot;The More You Know&quot; things that it can't hurt for Storytellers to keep in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T23:52:43-07:00","id":141285,"title":"","content":"Disquiet can be, optionally, combated with appropriate powers: Mental Resistance, cool heads prevail, miles away, a positive use of 'everyone knows,&quot; force relationship, sermon, demons have several tricks that can either protect the demon or mitigate disquiet in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T14:42:34-07:00","id":141822,"title":"","content":"&quot; While addictive, Vitae carries a far more sinister effect for<br /> those who drink it: the blood bond. A blood bond, also called a<br /> Vinculum, is a strand of powerful, one-sided emotion borne of<br /> Vitae. &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot; The Bond in Play<br /> Any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae, it<br /> creates or reinforces a blood bond. The bond comes in three<br /> stages, usually at the first, second, and third drinks. &quot;<br /> <br /> That should answer the blood bond question. They are affected. Everything is. They wouldn't have to show it if they didn't want to as that's an emotional thing, but they would have to feel it and act like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  Added second quote 05-18-2014, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T22:54:56-07:00","id":143122,"title":"","content":"An easy out for Disquiet Effects on Demons is based on a little note that says Spirits are not affected by Disquiet. Being Former-Spirits, you could just as easily rule Demons give the Finger to Disquiet, metaphysically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:58:17-07:00","id":143155,"title":"","content":"Nevermind they could be hysterically hating the Promethean for no apparently reason... and simply chose on to act on that feeling, in any way, shape or form. Because they're quantum machines with calculated feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}